  "title": "Env race makes terminal_formatting cc key test fail under the full suite",
  "type": "defect",
  "evidence": "(a) No REQ/ADR exists for kache in this tracker (pm db was empty). Gap: compiler::cc::tests::terminal_formatting_shares_cc_keys_with_cold_and_warm_probes compares cc cache keys computed at different times without holding process_state_test_lock, while sibling tests change the env vars the key reads.\n(b) src/compiler/cc/tests.rs:250 (asserts :295 cold, :299 warm). Key reads env at call time: src/compiler/cc.rs:4389 (cc_prefix_maps reads KACHE_CC_PATH_NORMALIZE, KACHE_BASE_DIR, SDKROOT, OUT_DIR at :4402-4411; again at :4445, :4449, :4458, :4650); maps hashed at cc.rs:6933 and :7108. Lock-holding writers: src/compiler/cc/tests.rs:6976 (include_dir_digest_exempts_an_existing_sdkroot_directory sets SDKROOT at :6985, removes at :6990) and :7962 (out_dir_and_sdk_maps_follow_the_environment_and_the_normalize_switch). The lock (src/test_support.rs:83) serialises writers only.\n(c) Unforced: `./scripts/with-test-resources.sh cargo test -q --bin kache` failed 3/40 (Opus, loads 21.6-31.0); cc module alone 10/100; owner's `just check` on 2026-10-14 failed once; Sol's full run R01 failed once at 16 threads. Forced, byte-identical to the owner's failure (Opus patch opus/instrumentation.diff): `env -u OUT_DIR FLAKY_FORCE_SDKROOT=/tmp/flaky-sdk <kache unit-test bin> --exact compiler::cc::tests::terminal_formatting_shares_cc_keys_with_cold_and_warm_probes` 2/2 fail:\npanicked at src/compiler/cc/tests.rs:299:9 (HEAD :295)\n  left: \"6a5dd9ebc2a33d878f7a0ea2cb8942db35b71cc3b4bbf8aca8d1ea4a8d5ae4d7\"\n right: \"ec170f0d4c633cc97b1a38b9c75e0ee2cbe2781647e22b1dca0817e436d3899a\"\nHash map (Opus): ec170f0d = OUT_DIR unset, SDKROOT unset; 6a5dd9eb = OUT_DIR unset, SDKROOT set; 23e919aa = cargo-style OUT_DIR set; 5503f180 = both set. Sol forced it independently by removing SDKROOT or toggling KACHE_CC_PATH_NORMALIZE mid-test (sol/instrumentation-phase*.patch, `KACHE_FLAKY_PROBE=SDKROOT|NORMALIZE`).",
  "resolution_plan": "Pass an environment snapshot (OUT_DIR, SDKROOT, KACHE_BASE_DIR, KACHE_CC_PATH_NORMALIZE, cwd) into cc_prefix_maps through KeyCtx, and have the test pin that snapshot. Minimal alternative: hold process_state_test_lock and pin the four vars with set_env_for_test before computing the baseline.",
